# [[ project_name ]]

A production-ready Django project generated with [djinit](https://github.com/S4NKALP/djinit) (`[[ architecture ]]` architecture, `[[ database_type ]]` database).

## Features

- **Environment-Split Settings**: Dedicated `base.py`, `development.py`, and `production.py` configurations via `django-environ`
- **REST API & JWT Auth**: Pre-configured Django REST Framework with `djangorestframework-simplejwt` token endpoints
- **Zero-Config SEO**: Built-in `/sitemap.xml` (`django.contrib.sitemaps`), `/robots.txt`, and `seo_context` processor (`SITE_NAME`, `SITE_DESCRIPTION`, canonical URLs)
- **Production Deployment Ready**: Includes `Dockerfile`, `docker-compose.yml`, `Procfile`, `runtime.txt`, `passenger_wsgi.py`, and WhiteNoise static serving
# @IF use_tailwind
- **Tailwind CSS**: Configured with `django-tailwind-cli` and DaisyUI
# @ENDIF
# @IF use_htmx
- **HTMX**: Configured with `django-htmx` middleware and partial rendering support
# @ENDIF
# @IF use_vite
- **Vite**: Configured with `django-vite` for modern frontend asset bundling
# @ENDIF

# @IF app_list
## Registered Apps

Registered in `[[ module_name ]]/settings/base.py`:

# @LOOP app in app_list
- `[[ app ]]`
# @ENDLOOP

> Tip: Add new architecture-aware apps anytime with `djinit app <app_name>`.

# @ENDIF
## Quick Start

### 1. Using `just` (Recommended)

1. Copy `.env.sample` to `.env` and review your environment variables:
   ```bash
   cp .env.sample .env
   ```
2. Run initial setup (installs dependencies, runs migrations, creates superuser):
   ```bash
   just setup
   ```
3. Start the development server:
   ```bash
   just dev
   ```

### 2. Using `uv` or `pip`

```bash
# Install dependencies (uv)
uv sync
# Or using pip
pip install -r requirements.txt

# Configure environment
cp .env.sample .env

# Apply migrations & create superuser
python manage.py migrate
python manage.py createsuperuser

# Start development server
python manage.py runserver
```

### 3. Using Docker

```bash
cp .env.sample .env
docker compose up --build
```

## Built-in Endpoints

| Endpoint | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `/admin/` | Django Admin (styled with Jazzmin) |
| `/token/` | Obtain JWT access & refresh pair |
| `/token/refresh/` | Refresh JWT access token |
| `/token/blacklist/` | Blacklist a refresh token |
| `/sitemap.xml` | XML sitemap (`StaticViewSitemap` in `[[ module_name ]]/sitemaps.py`) |
| `/robots.txt` | Crawler directives pointing to `/sitemap.xml` |

## Available `just` Commands

Run `just` to list all tasks:

| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `just dev` | Start Django development server |
| `just migrate` | Apply database migrations |
| `just makemigrations` | Generate new database migrations |
| `just createsuperuser` | Create an admin superuser |
| `just test` | Run test suite |
| `just test-coverage` | Run tests with coverage report |
| `just lint` | Run linter checks |
| `just format` | Format codebase |
| `just ci` | Run all linting and check tasks |
| `just shell` | Open Django interactive shell |
| `just clean` | Clean temporary cache files |
| `just server` | Start production WSGI server |

